    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31677" root="غرض" body-key="g">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غرّض</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَغْرِيضٌ</span>, <i>He ate fresh flesh-meat.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَرَضَ</span>, in two places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
One says also, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَرِّضْ فِى سِقَائَكَ</span> <i>Fill not thy skin</i>
[<i>completely; leave a portion unfilled in thy skin</i>].
(S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُلَانٌ بَحْرٌ لَا يُغَرَّضُ</span> i. e. [<i>Such a one
is a sea</i>] <i>that will not become exhausted.</i> (S, A, TA.) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غرّض</span> signifies also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفَكَّهَ</span>, (K, TA.)
[meaning <i>He affected jesting,</i> or <i>joking,</i> for it
is] said in the I. to be from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الفُكَاهَةُ</span> signifying
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المُزَاحُ</span>. (TA.)

